    "ice_wall": {
        "note": "A wall of ice on the switchbacks; Ryn learns Blaze and melts it.",
        "lock": false,
        "beats": [
            {
                "after": 5,
                "pace": "slow",
                "text": "The path round the last turn is gone. A wall of blue ice, thick as a house, fills the gap between the rock faces, and in its heart something has been caught and looks back at you without any interest at all. It is not a wall made by weather."
            },
            {
                "after": 5,
                "pace": "slow",
                "text": "[[YELLOW]]Ryn speaks:[[/]] [[GREEN]]\"It is only cold. Cold is only the absence of something. Wait. I think I know what goes in the gap.\"[[/]]"
            },
            {
                "after": 5,
                "pace": "slow",
                "text": "She stands with her small hands out and her eyes shut, and nothing happens, and nothing, and then the air above her knuckles goes the colour of a struck match. She laughs once, astonished. The ember she has always carried is, quite suddenly, a fire.",
                "effects": {
                    "teach_companion": {
                        "npc": "ryn_young",
                        "spell": "blaze"
                    }
                }
            },
            {
                "after": 4,
                "pace": "slow",
                "text": "The ice goes the way a held breath goes. It weeps, and runs, and cracks from the middle outward with a sound like a river starting, and then it is a hundred small waterfalls down the rock and the path is open.",
                "effects": {
                    "set_flag": "ice_melted"
                }
            }
        ]
    },
